   "stem": {
      "text": "Find the radius of convergence of the power series \\( \\sum_{n=2}^{\\infty} \\frac{4 \\cdot 8^{n} \\left(x - 3\\right)^{n}}{n} \\).",
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "statement",
      "label": "\\( R = \\frac{1}{8} \\)"
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "For the ratio test, form \\( \\left|\\frac{a_{n+1}}{a_n}\\right| \\) from consecutive terms of \\( \\frac{4 \\cdot 8^{n} \\left(x - 3\\right)^{n}}{n} \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99042",
         "rule_named": "ratio of consecutive terms"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Its limit is \\( \\lim_{n\\to\\infty} \\left(\\frac{n}{n+1}\\right) 8 \\left|x - 3\\right| = 8 \\left|x - 3\\right| \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99043",
         "rule_named": "limit of the ratio"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The series converges when this limit is less than 1: \\( 8 \\left|x - 3\\right| < 1 \\), that is \\( \\left|x - 3\\right| < \\frac{1}{8} \\), so the radius of convergence is \\( R = \\frac{1}{8} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            8
         ],
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99047",
         "rule_named": "radius stated"
      }
   ],
